Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-02
Subject: Initialize exception state record fields explicitly
License: expat

`tcgexceptionstatehandler.texceptionstate` contains only a label object
reference and two flow-control sets.  `Default(texceptionstate)` therefore
means a nil label and empty sets; spell those values out directly so the
bootstrap compiler source does not require the `Default` intrinsic here.

--- a/compiler/ncgflw.pas
+++ b/compiler/ncgflw.pas
@@ -714,7 +714,9 @@
          breaktrylabel:=nil;
          continueexceptlabel:=nil;
          breakexceptlabel:=nil;
-         doobjectdestroyandreraisestate:=Default(tcgexceptionstatehandler.texceptionstate);
+         doobjectdestroyandreraisestate.exceptionlabel:=nil;
+         doobjectdestroyandreraisestate.oldflowcontrol:=[];
+         doobjectdestroyandreraisestate.newflowcontrol:=[];
 
          { this can be called recursivly }
          oldBreakLabel:=nil;
